      "reviews": [
        {
          "author": "LB",
          "rating": 5,
          "text": "BACINO the Cozy Italian Gem in Pasir Panjang You Need to Try Immediately!\n\nTucked away in Pasir Panjang, BACINO is a warm, intimate Italian bistro that feels like a little slice of Italy right here in Singapore. Think delicious, authentic Italian cuisine paired with an impressive selection of wines — most of the ingredients and bottles are imported straight from Italy, which you can truly taste and appreciate in every dish and sip.\n\nI first met the owner back in 2024 at a nice Italian wine event. When our paths crossed again recently, I knew I had to check the place out with a couple of my good friends. We had a feeling the food and wine would be excellent… and YES, were we right!\n\nFrom the moment we walked in, we really like everything — the cosy ambience, the flavours on the plate, the drinks, the owner’s warm hospitality, and the attentive service team. It was so good that we ended up going back three times in one week. Sounds crazy? Maybe. But once you taste it for yourself, you’ll understand 🤭\n\nBACINO also has some really good lunch and drinks deals, so there’s never a bad time to drop by.\n\nDo yourself a favour and head over soon. You won’t be disappointed — in fact, you might just become a regular like us.",
          "relativeTime": "2 months ago",
          "profilePhoto": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjUul2EIe1s6OC8ibo0XU3hx2o1MCAQ5kMyWHX0O89LDhVppU0w=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba2"
        },
        {
          "author": "Kirby c",
          "rating": 5,
          "text": "The chef is serious about his food! So far the best Aglio olio i have ever had. Technique and execution of dish is chefs kiss, right amount of garlic, oil and heat. The emulsification is perfect which makes the sauce incredibly creamy.\nHave tried some of the other pasta dishes, they were pretty good as well but the star is definitely aglio olio\nCherry on top is the tiramisu which was part of the lunch set, strong coffee w generous sprinkle of cocoa powder, which was a great end to the meal\nEven though i dont really like just eating carbs for a meal, i would gladly come back for the aglio olio again.",
          "relativeTime": "2 weeks ago",
          "profilePhoto": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjXNiaWwclWwOZOyEJo7xZ--sfpIWn1uCR8sIZalO-WBNUSx-3o=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba4"
        },
        {
          "author": "Lis",
          "rating": 5,
          "text": "Hands down to the best carbonara in Singapore that i’ve had. Better than many big names in the centre. Don’t be fool as the chef is super clear about his food: it’s must be delicious and authentic. We love the risotto as well. Its deep seafood flavour is subtly hinted with acidic balance. Definitely worth a trip.",
          "relativeTime": "a month ago",
          "profilePhoto": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjW4aUSGdfbLcGmlZ9p56NPZO035H0Q_8l_ZtxRYIKrZ7Iw8pS4=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba4"
        },
        {
          "author": "Denise Ong",
          "rating": 5,
          "text": "Tried the porchetta, cacio e pepe and osso buco. Dessert was tiramisu. Would recommend the porchetta as a starter and definitely highly recommend the osso buco. The team shared with us that the meat was slow cooked over 6 hours and mashed potatoes were homemade. The taste of osso buco lingered in our mouth even after we had finished it. Goes well with red wine.",
          "relativeTime": "a month ago",
          "profilePhoto": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjVW5WgUHar_CnNbrhbV5Pvz78kDpCfemP-N_F_I46KxWiLermVt=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba5"
        },
        {
          "author": "Angie Glen (AC)",
          "rating": 5,
          "text": "This review came 10mths late, lol. I kept thinking about their carbonara whenever I had any unsatisfatory ones elsewhere.\n\nBrought my wife for a low-key birthday celebration last Nov end. She loves Italian cuisine and wanted to try long before it moved here. Started with bruschetta, squid ink risotto was great, and I had an unforgetable legit carbonara that I would gladly travel for an hour just to taste again. Sadly we're too full to order more but squeezed some space for their fantastic cannoli to round up the wonderful meal.\n\nHighly recommended to give it a try and we'll definitely drop by when we're in the area.",
          "relativeTime": "2 months ago",
          "profilePhoto": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjXBc_u43A-PHzitSR36ZaauA2wnRF9EpBlvsAxq8Lt4T3fuqyQ=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba3"
        }
      ]
    },
